SUMMARY:28 Katak 2083 · Katak Sudhi 4 (Chauth (Chaturthi)) (੨੮ ਕੱਤਕ ੨੦੮੩) — Gurgaddi SGGS Ji · Barsi Sant Jwala Singh Ji
DESCRIPTION:Desi Solar Date: 28 Katak\, Bikrami Sambat 2083 (੨੮ ਕੱਤਕ\, ਸੰਮਤ ੨੦੮੩)\nLunar Tithi: Katak Sudhi 4 (Chauth (Chaturthi)) · ਕੱਤਕ ਸੁਦੀ ੪ (ਚੌਥ)\nTithi ends (Sri Anandpur Sahib IST): 08:44 PM\, 13 Nov\n\nGurgaddi Divas — Sri Guru Granth Sahib Ji / ਗੁਰਗੱਦੀ ਦਿਵਸ — ਸ੍ਰੀ ਗੁਰੂ ਗ੍ਰੰਥ ਸਾਹਿਬ ਜੀ\nKatak Sudhi 4 (Chauth) · Sri Guru Gobind Singh Ji bestowed eternal Guruship upon Sri Guru Granth Sahib Ji at Sri Hazur Sahib\, Nanded (1765 Bikrami).\nSources: Bhatt Vahi Talauda (Pargana Jind) (Entry for Katak Sudhi 4\, Sambat 1765 Bikrami · Testimony of Narbud Singh Bhatt) | Rehatnama Bhai Prahlad Singh & Panth Prakash (Aagya Bhaee Akaal Kee — Eternal Guruship Colophon)\n\nBarsi — Sant Baba Jwala Singh Ji (Harkhowal) / ਬਰਸੀ — ਸੰਤ ਬਾਬਾ ਜਵਾਲਾ ਸਿੰਘ ਜੀ (ਹਰਖੋਵਾਲ)\nKatak Sudhi 4 (28 Katak\, Sambat 2083) · Annual Barsi of Brahmgyani Sant Baba Jwala Singh Ji Harkhowal (1889–1957 CE)\, luminary of Hoti Mardan Samparda.\nSources: Sri Guru Granth Sahib Ji (Ang 273 · Sukhmani Sahib (Ashtpadi 8))\n\nhttps://calendar.tatkhalsa.in/
CATEGORIES:Tat Khalsa Puratan Jantri\,Daily Bikrami\,GURPURAB\,BARSI
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
