SUMMARY:29 Maghar 2083 · Maghar Sudhi 5 (Panchmi) (੨੯ ਮੱਘਰ ੨੦੮੩) — Shaheedi Guru Tegh Bahadur Ji · Baba Fateh Singh Ji Janam · Bhai Mati Das\, Sati Das & Dayala Ji
DESCRIPTION:Desi Solar Date: 29 Maghar\, Bikrami Sambat 2083 (੨੯ ਮੱਘਰ\, ਸੰਮਤ ੨੦੮੩)\nLunar Tithi: Maghar Sudhi 5 (Panchmi) · ਮੱਘਰ ਸੁਦੀ ੫ (ਪੰਚਮੀ)\nTithi ends (Sri Anandpur Sahib IST): 07:17 PM\, 14 Dec\n\nShaheedi Divas — Sri Guru Tegh Bahadur Ji & Three Beloved Sikhs / ਸ਼ਹੀਦੀ ਦਿਵਸ — ਸ੍ਰੀ ਗੁਰੂ ਤੇਗ਼ ਬਹਾਦਰ ਜੀ\, ਭਾਈ ਮਤੀ ਦਾਸ\, ਭਾਈ ਸਤੀ ਦਾਸ ਤੇ ਭਾਈ ਦਿਆਲਾ ਜੀ\nMaghar Sudhi 5 (29 Maghar\, Sambat 2083) · Supreme martyrdom of the Ninth Patshah at Chandni Chowk\, Delhi in defense of dharam and freedom of conscience (Maghar Sudhi 5\, 1732 Bikrami).\nSources: Sri Dasam Granth Sahib Ji (Bachitar Natak) (Adhyay 5\, Chhand 13–15 · Tilak Janju Rakha Prabh Taaka) | Bhatt Vahi Multani Sindhi (Maghar Sudhi 5\, Sambat 1732 · Witness record of Delhi Shaheedi)\n\nParkash Purab — Sahibzada Baba Fateh Singh Ji / ਪ੍ਰਕਾਸ਼ ਪੁਰਬ — ਸਾਹਿਬਜ਼ਾਦਾ ਬਾਬਾ ਫ਼ਤਹਿ ਸਿੰਘ ਜੀ\n29 Maghar\, Sambat 2083 (11 Phagun alternate tradition noted) · Commemorating the birth of youngest Sahibzada Baba Fateh Singh Ji at Sri Anandpur Sahib (Sambat 1755 Bikrami)\, symbol of fearless Khalsa sovereignty.\nSources: Bhatt Vahi Multani Sindhi & Guru Kian Sakhian (Sambat 1755 · Sri Anandpur Sahib Birth Record)\n\nShaheedi Divas — Bhai Mati Das Ji\, Bhai Sati Das Ji & Bhai Dayala Ji / ਸ਼ਹੀਦੀ ਦਿਵਸ — ਭਾਈ ਮਤੀ ਦਾਸ ਜੀ\, ਭਾਈ ਸਤੀ ਦਾਸ ਜੀ ਅਤੇ ਭਾਈ ਦਿਆਲਾ ਜੀ\nMaghar Sudhi 5 (29 Maghar\, Sambat 2083 · Chandni Chowk) · Unmatched martyrdom of Bhai Mati Das Ji (sawn alive reciting Japji Sahib)\, Bhai Dayala Ji (boiled in a cauldron)\, and Bhai Sati Das Ji (wrapped in cotton and set aflame) before Sri Guru Tegh Bahadur Sahib Ji in Delhi.\nSources: Bhatt Vahi Talauda & Sri Gur Pratap Suraj Granth (Raas 12\, Ansu 44–52 · Chandni Chowk Martyrs (Sambat 1732))\n\nhttps://calendar.tatkhalsa.in/
CATEGORIES:Tat Khalsa Puratan Jantri\,Daily Bikrami\,SHAHEEDI\,GURPURAB
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
