UID:daily-2026-12-20@calendar.tatkhalsa.in
DTSTAMP:20260314T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261220
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261221
SUMMARY:5 Poh 2083 · Maghar Sudhi 11 (Ekadashi) (੫ ਪੋਹ ੨੦੮੩) — Mata Jito Ji Joti Jot
DESCRIPTION:Desi Solar Date: 5 Poh\, Bikrami Sambat 2083 (੫ ਪੋਹ\, ਸੰਮਤ ੨੦੮੩)\nLunar Tithi: Maghar Sudhi 11 (Ekadashi) · ਮੱਘਰ ਸੁਦੀ ੧੧ (ਇਕਾਦਸ਼ੀ)\nTithi ends (Sri Anandpur Sahib IST): 08:16 PM\, 20 Dec\n\nJoti Jot Divas — Mata Jito Ji (Sri Anandpur Sahib) / ਜੋਤੀ ਜੋਤ ਦਿਵਸ — ਮਾਤਾ ਜੀਤੋ ਜੀ (ਸ੍ਰੀ ਅਨੰਦਪੁਰ ਸਾਹਿਬ)\n5 Poh\, Sambat 2083 (Poh Sudhi 5\, Sambat 1757) · Passing of Mata Jito Ji (mother of Sahibzade Baba Jujhar Singh Ji\, Baba Zorawar Singh Ji & Baba Fateh Singh Ji) at Sri Anandpur Sahib (Agampura).\nSources: Bhatt Vahi & Guru Kian Sakhian (5 Poh\, Sambat 1757 · Agampura\, Sri Anandpur Sahib)\n\nhttps://calendar.tatkhalsa.in/
CATEGORIES:Tat Khalsa Puratan Jantri\,Daily Bikrami\,KHALSA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:daily-2026-12-21@calendar.tatkhalsa.in
DTSTAMP:20260314T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261221
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261222
SUMMARY:6 Poh 2083 · Maghar Sudhi 12 (Dwadashi) (੬ ਪੋਹ ੨੦੮੩) — Anandpur Qila Chhodna
DESCRIPTION:Desi Solar Date: 6 Poh\, Bikrami Sambat 2083 (੬ ਪੋਹ\, ਸੰਮਤ ੨੦੮੩)\nLunar Tithi: Maghar Sudhi 12 (Dwadashi) · ਮੱਘਰ ਸੁਦੀ ੧੨ (ਦੁਆਦਸ਼ੀ)\nTithi ends (Sri Anandpur Sahib IST): 05:38 PM\, 21 Dec\n\nShaheedi Hafta — Sri Anandpur Sahib Qila Chhodna (6–7 Poh) / ਸ਼ਹੀਦੀ ਹਫ਼ਤਾ — ਸ੍ਰੀ ਅਨੰਦਪੁਰ ਸਾਹਿਬ ਕਿਲ੍ਹਾ ਛੱਡਣਾ (੬–੭ ਪੋਹ)\n6 Poh\, Sambat 2083 (Night of 6–7 Poh\, Sambat 1761) · Opening of Shaheedi Hafta: after an eight-month siege\, Sri Guru Gobind Singh Ji\, the Guru Ghar Parivar\, and the Khalsa evacuated Qila Anandgarh on the freezing night of 6–7 Poh\, Sambat 1761.\nSources: Bhatt Vahi Talauda & Prachin Panth Prakash (6–7 Poh\, Sambat 1761 · Evacuation of Qila Anandgarh)\n\nhttps://calendar.tatkhalsa.in/
CATEGORIES:Tat Khalsa Puratan Jantri\,Daily Bikrami\,SHAHEEDI
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:daily-2026-12-22@calendar.tatkhalsa.in
DTSTAMP:20260314T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261222
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261223
SUMMARY:7 Poh 2083 · Maghar Sudhi 13 (Teras (Trayodashi)) (੭ ਪੋਹ ੨੦੮੩) — Janam Baba Atal Sahib Ji · Sarsa Nadi & Bhai Uday/Bachittar Singh
DESCRIPTION:Desi Solar Date: 7 Poh\, Bikrami Sambat 2083 (੭ ਪੋਹ\, ਸੰਮਤ ੨੦੮੩)\nLunar Tithi: Maghar Sudhi 13 (Teras (Trayodashi)) · ਮੱਘਰ ਸੁਦੀ ੧੩ (ਤੇਰਸ)\nTithi ends (Sri Anandpur Sahib IST): 02:25 PM\, 22 Dec\n\nJanam Divas — Baba Atal Rai Sahib Ji / ਜਨਮ ਦਿਹਾੜਾ — ਬਾਬਾ ਅਟੱਲ ਰਾਇ ਸਾਹਿਬ ਜੀ\nMaghar Sudhi 13 (7 Poh\, Sambat 2083) · Birth commemoration of Baba Atal Rai Ji (1676 Bikrami)\, luminous son of Sri Guru Hargobind Sahib Ji and Mata Nanaki Ji\, honored by the nine-story Gurdwara Baba Atal Sahib.\nSources: Sri Gurpratap Suraj Granth Sahib Ji (Raas 6\, Ansu 38–42 · Janam & Spiritual Glory of Baba Atal Rai Ji)\n\nShaheedi Hafta — Sarsa Nadi Vichhora\, Bhai Uday Singh Ji & Bhai Bachittar Singh Ji / ਸ਼ਹੀਦੀ ਹਫ਼ਤਾ — ਸਰਸਾ ਨਦੀ ਵਿਛੋੜਾ\, ਭਾਈ ਉਦੈ ਸਿੰਘ ਜੀ ਅਤੇ ਭਾਈ ਬਚਿੱਤਰ ਸਿੰਘ ਜੀ\n7 Poh\, Sambat 2083 (Parivar Vichhora & Shahi Tibbi) · Separation of Guru Gobind Singh Ji’s family at the flooded Sarsa River (Parivar Vichhora)\, Asa Di Vaar amid battle\, and the legendary martyrdom of Bhai Uday Singh Ji (Shahi Tibbi) and Bhai Bachittar Singh Ji (Malikpur/Kotla Nihang).\nSources: Bhatt Vahi Multani Sindhi & Sri Gur Pratap Suraj Granth (Ayan 2\, Ansu 1–12 · Sarsa Nadi\, Shahi Tibbi & Kotla Nihang (7 Poh 1761))\n\nhttps://calendar.tatkhalsa.in/
CATEGORIES:Tat Khalsa Puratan Jantri\,Daily Bikrami\,GURPURAB\,SHAHEEDI
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:daily-2026-12-23@calendar.tatkhalsa.in
DTSTAMP:20260314T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261223
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261224
SUMMARY:8 Poh 2083 · Maghar Puranmashi (੮ ਪੋਹ ੨੦੮੩) — Shaheedi Vadde Sahibzade · Three Panj Pyare (Chamkaur)
DESCRIPTION:Desi Solar Date: 8 Poh\, Bikrami Sambat 2083 (੮ ਪੋਹ\, ਸੰਮਤ ੨੦੮੩)\nLunar Tithi: Maghar Sudhi 15 (Puranmashi) · ਮੱਘਰ ਸੁਦੀ ੧੫ (ਪੂਰਨਮਾਸ਼ੀ)\nTithi ends (Sri Anandpur Sahib IST): 07:00 AM\, 24 Dec\n\nShaheedi Divas — Vadde Sahibzade (Sri Chamkaur Sahib) / ਸ਼ਹੀਦੀ ਦਿਵਸ — ਵੱਡੇ ਸਾਹਿਬਜ਼ਾਦੇ (ਸ੍ਰੀ ਚਮਕੌਰ ਸਾਹਿਬ)\n8 Poh (Sambat 2083) · Martyrdom of Baba Ajit Singh Ji\, Baba Jujhar Singh Ji\, and the Singhs of Garhi Chamkaur (8 Poh\, 1761 Bikrami).\nSources: Sri Dasam Granth Sahib Ji (Zafarnama) (Verses 19–22 & 78 · Battle of Chamkaur & Four Sons) | Prachin Panth Prakash (Rattan Singh Bhangu) (Sakhi Garhi Chamkaur · 8 Poh 1761 Bikrami)\n\nShaheedi Divas — Three Panj Pyare (Bhai Himmat Singh\, Bhai Mohkam Singh & Bhai Sahib Singh Ji) / ਸ਼ਹੀਦੀ ਦਿਵਸ — ਤਿੰਨ ਪੰਜ ਪਿਆਰੇ (ਭਾਈ ਹਿੰਮਤ ਸਿੰਘ\, ਭਾਈ ਮੋਹਕਮ ਸਿੰਘ ਅਤੇ ਭਾਈ ਸਾਹਿਬ ਸਿੰਘ ਜੀ)\n8 Poh\, Sambat 2083 (Battle of Sri Chamkaur Sahib) · Supreme martyrdom of three of the original Panj Pyare—Bhai Himmat Singh Ji (Jagannath Puri)\, Bhai Mohkam Singh Ji (Dwarka)\, and Bhai Sahib Singh Ji (Bidar)—alongside the Vadde Sahibzade and 40 Singhs at Garhi Chamkaur.\nSources: Bhatt Vahi Talauda & Prachin Panth Prakash (8 Poh\, Sambat 1761 · Garhi Sri Chamkaur Sahib Martyrs)\n\nhttps://calendar.tatkhalsa.in/
CATEGORIES:Tat Khalsa Puratan Jantri\,Daily Bikrami\,Puranmashi\,SHAHEEDI
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
