SUMMARY:1 Vaisakh 2084 · Chet Sudhi 8 (Ashtami) (੧ ਵੈਸਾਖ ੨੦੮੪) — Vaisakh Sangrand · Vaisakhi · Khalsa Sajna · Panj Pyare & Raj Tilak
DESCRIPTION:Desi Solar Date: 1 Vaisakh\, Bikrami Sambat 2084 (੧ ਵੈਸਾਖ\, ਸੰਮਤ ੨੦੮੪)\nLunar Tithi: Chet Sudhi 8 (Ashtami) · ਚੇਤ ਸੁਦੀ ੮ (ਅਸ਼ਟਮੀ)\nTithi ends (Sri Anandpur Sahib IST): 03:25 PM\, 14 Apr\nSangrand: 1 Vaisakh (ਵੈਸਾਖ ਸੰਗਰਾਂਦ) · Sankranti at 09:00 AM\, 14 Apr IST\n\nVaisakhi — 328th Khalsa Sajna Divas / ਵੈਸਾਖੀ — ੩੨੮ਵਾਂ ਖ਼ਾਲਸਾ ਸਾਜਨਾ ਦਿਵਸ\n1 Vaisakh\, Sambat 2084 (Mesha Sankranti) · Creation of the Khalsa Panth and Khande-ki-Pahul by Sri Guru Gobind Singh Ji at Takht Sri Kesgarh Sahib on 1 Vaisakh\, 1756 Bikrami.\nSources: Sri Gur Sobha (Kavi Sainapati) (Adhyay 5 · Vaisakh Sangrand 1756 Bikrami Khalsa Prakat) | Sri Dasam Granth Sahib Ji (Khalsa Mehma) (33 Swaiye & Khalsa Mehma · Sovereign Identity of the Khalsa)\n\nPanj Pyare (Bhai Dharam Singh Ji) & Maharaja Ranjit Singh Ji Raj Tilak (1 Vaisakh) / ਪੰਜ ਪਿਆਰੇ (ਭਾਈ ਧਰਮ ਸਿੰਘ ਜੀ) ਅਤੇ ਮਹਾਰਾਜਾ ਰਣਜੀਤ ਸਿੰਘ ਜੀ ਰਾਜ-ਤਿਲਕ (੧ ਵੈਸਾਖ)\n1 Vaisakh\, Sambat 2084 (Vaisakhi — Sambat 1756 & 1858) · Honoring all Five Beloved Ones (Bhai Daya Singh\, Bhai Dharam Singh\, Bhai Himmat Singh\, Bhai Mohkam Singh & Bhai Sahib Singh Ji) consecrated on Vaisakhi 1699\, and Maharaja Ranjit Singh Ji’s Raj Tilak at Lahore (1 Vaisakh\, Sambat 1858).\nSources: Mahan Kosh & Prachin Panth Prakash (1 Vaisakh 1756 (Panj Pyare) & 1 Vaisakh 1858 (Maharaja Ranjit Singh Raj Tilak))\n\nhttps://calendar.tatkhalsa.in/
CATEGORIES:Tat Khalsa Puratan Jantri\,Daily Bikrami\,Sangrand\,KHALSA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
