SUMMARY:11 Harh 2084 · Harh Vadhi 6 (Chhat (Shashthi)) (੧੧ ਹਾੜ੍ਹ ੨੦੮੪) — Parkash Guru Hargobind Ji · Baba Banda Singh Bahadur
DESCRIPTION:Desi Solar Date: 11 Harh\, Bikrami Sambat 2084 (੧੧ ਹਾੜ੍ਹ\, ਸੰਮਤ ੨੦੮੪)\nLunar Tithi: Harh Vadhi 6 (Chhat (Shashthi)) · ਹਾੜ੍ਹ ਵਦੀ ੬ (ਛਠ)\nTithi ends (Sri Anandpur Sahib IST): 08:19 PM\, 25 Jun\n\nParkash Purab — Sri Guru Hargobind Sahib Ji / ਪ੍ਰਕਾਸ਼ ਪੁਰਬ — ਸ੍ਰੀ ਗੁਰੂ ਹਰਿਗੋਬਿੰਦ ਸਾਹਿਬ ਜੀ\nHarh Vadhi 6 (11 Harh\, Sambat 2084) · Parkash Purab of Sixth Patshah\, Master of Miri-Piri and founder of Sri Akal Takht Sahib (Guru Ki Wadali\, 1652 Bikrami).\nSources: Sri Guru Granth Sahib Ji (Ang 396 · Raag Aasa Mahalla 5 (Satgur Saache Diya Bhej)) | Gurbilas Patshahi 6 (Adhyay 1 · Wadali Parkash & Miri-Piri)\n\nShaheedi Divas — Baba Banda Singh Bahadur & 740 Khalsa Shaheeds (Mehrauli\, Delhi) / ਸ਼ਹੀਦੀ ਦਿਵਸ — ਬਾਬਾ ਬੰਦਾ ਸਿੰਘ ਬਹਾਦਰ ਅਤੇ ੭੪੦ ਖ਼ਾਲਸਾ ਸ਼ਹੀਦ (ਮਹਿਰੌਲੀ\, ਦਿੱਲੀ)\n11 Harh\, Sambat 2084 (Harh Vadhi 7 / 9 June 1716) · Martyrdom of Baba Banda Singh Bahadur\, his four-year-old son Baba Ajai Singh Ji\, and companion Singhs at Mehrauli\, Delhi (Sambat 1773) after establishing the first sovereign Khalsa Raj.\nSources: Prachin Panth Prakash (Bhai Rattan Singh Bhangu) (Banda Singh Bahadur Shaheedi Prasang · Harh Sambat 1773)\n\nhttps://calendar.tatkhalsa.in/
CATEGORIES:Tat Khalsa Puratan Jantri\,Daily Bikrami\,GURPURAB\,SHAHEEDI
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
