DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270902
SUMMARY:16 Bhadon 2084 · Bhadon Sudhi 1 (Ekam (Pratipada)) (੧੬ ਭਾਦੋਂ ੨੦੮੪) — Pehla Parkash SGGS Ji · 6 Bhagat Sahibaan (SGGS) · Bhai Satta & Balwand Ji
DESCRIPTION:Desi Solar Date: 16 Bhadon\, Bikrami Sambat 2084 (੧੬ ਭਾਦੋਂ\, ਸੰਮਤ ੨੦੮੪)\nLunar Tithi: Bhadon Sudhi 1 (Ekam (Pratipada)) · ਭਾਦੋਂ ਸੁਦੀ ੧ (ਏਕਮ)\nTithi ends (Sri Anandpur Sahib IST): 07:52 PM\, 1 Sept\n\nPehla Parkash Purab — Sri Guru Granth Sahib Ji / ਪਹਿਲਾ ਪ੍ਰਕਾਸ਼ ਪੁਰਬ — ਸ੍ਰੀ ਗੁਰੂ ਗ੍ਰੰਥ ਸਾਹਿਬ ਜੀ\nBhadon Sudhi 1 (16 Bhadon\, Sambat 2084) · First installation of Adi Sri Guru Granth Sahib Ji at Sachkhand Sri Harmandir Sahib by Sri Guru Arjan Dev Ji (Bhadon Sudhi 1\, 1661 Bikrami).\nSources: Kartarpur Bir Colophon (Tatkara) (Sambat 1661 Miti Bhadon Vadi 1 (Completion) & Sudhi 1 (Installation)) | Sri Gur Pratap Suraj Granth (Raas 3\, Ansu 48–50 · First Hukamnama (Suhee Mahalla 5))\n\nBhagat Bani Commemoration — Bhagat Trilochan\, Beni\, Bhikhan\, Sadhna\, Parmanand & Surdas Ji / ਭਗਤ ਬਾਣੀ ਯਾਦਗਾਰ — ਭਗਤ ਤ੍ਰਿਲੋਚਨ\, ਬੇਣੀ\, ਭੀਖਨ\, ਸਧਨਾ\, ਪਰਮਾਨੰਦ ਅਤੇ ਸੂਰਦਾਸ ਜੀ\n16 Bhadon\, Sambat 2084 (Pehla Parkash SGGS · Mahan Kosh Note) · Commemorating the six SGGS Bhagat Sahibaan whose exact birth days are unrecorded in Puratan chronicles: Bhagat Trilochan Ji (Ang 92\, 525\, 695)\, Bhagat Beni Ji (Ang 93\, 489\, 1351)\, Bhagat Bhikhan Ji (Ang 659)\, Bhagat Sadhna Ji (Ang 858)\, Bhagat Parmanand Ji (Ang 1253)\, and Bhagat Surdas Ji (Ang 1253).\nSources: Sri Guru Granth Sahib Ji (Ang 92\, 93\, 489\, 525\, 659\, 695\, 858\, 1253\, 1351 · Bhagat Bani) | Mahan Kosh (Bhai Kahn Singh Nabha) (Entries: Trilochan\, Beni\, Bhikhan\, Sadhna\, Parmanand\, Surdas)\n\nGursikh Bani-kars — Bhai Satta Ji & Bhai Balwand Ji (Ramkali Ki Vaar\, SGGS Ang 966) / ਗੁਰਸਿੱਖ ਬਾਣੀਕਾਰ — ਭਾਈ ਸੱਤਾ ਜੀ ਅਤੇ ਭਾਈ ਬਲਵੰਡ ਜੀ (ਰਾਮਕਲੀ ਕੀ ਵਾਰ\, ਅੰਗ ੯੬੬)\n16 Bhadon\, Sambat 2084 (Pehla Parkash SGGS · Mahan Kosh Note) · Honoring court Rababis and SGGS Gursikh Bani-kars Bhai Satta Ji & Bhai Balwand Ji\, authors of Ramkali Ki Vaar (Tikke Di Vaar\, Ang 966–968) praising the Guru Gaddi succession.\nSources: Sri Guru Granth Sahib Ji (Ang 966–968 · Ramkali Ki Vaar (Rai Balwand & Satta Doom))\n\nhttps://calendar.tatkhalsa.in/
CATEGORIES:Tat Khalsa Puratan Jantri\,Daily Bikrami\,GURPURAB\,KHALSA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
