UID:daily-2027-09-25@calendar.tatkhalsa.in
DTSTAMP:20260314T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270926
SUMMARY:9 Assu 2084 · Assu Vadhi 10 (Dasmi (Dashami)) (੯ ਅੱਸੂ ੨੦੮੪) — Joti Jot Guru Nanak Dev Ji · Guru Nanak Dev Ji Parivar
DESCRIPTION:Desi Solar Date: 9 Assu\, Bikrami Sambat 2084 (੯ ਅੱਸੂ\, ਸੰਮਤ ੨੦੮੪)\nLunar Tithi: Assu Vadhi 10 (Dasmi (Dashami)) · ਅੱਸੂ ਵਦੀ ੧੦ (ਦਸਮੀ)\nTithi ends (Sri Anandpur Sahib IST): 10:33 PM\, 25 Sept\n\nJoti Jot Divas — Sri Guru Nanak Dev Ji (Sri Kartarpur Sahib) / ਜੋਤੀ ਜੋਤ ਦਿਵਸ — ਸ੍ਰੀ ਗੁਰੂ ਨਾਨਕ ਦੇਵ ਜੀ (ਸ੍ਰੀ ਕਰਤਾਰਪੁਰ ਸਾਹਿਬ)\nAssu Vadhi 10 (9 Assu\, Sambat 2084) · Sri Guru Nanak Dev Ji merged into the Eternal Light at Sri Kartarpur Sahib on Assu Vadhi 10\, Sambat 1596 Bikrami.\nSources: Puratan Janamsakhi (Colebrooke / Walayatwali) (Colophon of Sambat 1596 Assu Vadi 10 · Kartarpur Sahib)\n\nGuru Ghar Heritage — Bebe Nanaki Ji\, Mata Sulakhni Ji & Baba Lakhmi Das Ji / ਗੁਰੂ ਘਰ ਵਿਰਾਸਤ — ਬੇਬੇ ਨਾਨਕੀ ਜੀ\, ਮਾਤਾ ਸੁਲੱਖਣੀ ਜੀ ਅਤੇ ਬਾਬਾ ਲਖਮੀ ਦਾਸ ਜੀ\n9 Assu\, Sambat 2084 (On Sri Guru Nanak Dev Ji Joti Jot) · Honoring Sri Guru Nanak Dev Ji’s sacred family: elder sister Bebe Nanaki Ji (first to recognize Guru Nanak’s divinity)\, consort Mata Sulakhni Ji (Batala & Kartarpur Sahib)\, and younger Sahibzada Baba Lakhmi Das Ji.\nSources: Puratan Janamsakhi & Mahan Kosh (Entries: Bebe Nanaki Ji\, Mata Sulakhni Ji & Baba Lakhmi Das Ji)\n\nhttps://calendar.tatkhalsa.in/
CATEGORIES:Tat Khalsa Puratan Jantri\,Daily Bikrami\,GURPURAB\,KHALSA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
