SUMMARY:17 Maghar 2084 · Maghar Sudhi 5 (Panchmi) (੧੭ ਮੱਘਰ ੨੦੮੪) — Shaheedi Guru Tegh Bahadur Ji · Baba Budha Ji Joti Jot · Bhai Mati Das\, Sati Das & Dayala Ji
DESCRIPTION:Desi Solar Date: 17 Maghar\, Bikrami Sambat 2084 (੧੭ ਮੱਘਰ\, ਸੰਮਤ ੨੦੮੪)\nLunar Tithi: Maghar Sudhi 5 (Panchmi) · ਮੱਘਰ ਸੁਦੀ ੫ (ਪੰਚਮੀ)\nTithi ends (Sri Anandpur Sahib IST): 04:15 PM\, 3 Dec\n\nShaheedi Divas — Sri Guru Tegh Bahadur Ji / ਸ਼ਹੀਦੀ ਦਿਵਸ — ਸ੍ਰੀ ਗੁਰੂ ਤੇਗ਼ ਬਹਾਦਰ ਜੀ\nMaghar Sudhi 5 (17 Maghar\, Sambat 2084) · Martyrdom of the Ninth Patshah at Chandni Chowk\, Delhi on Maghar Sudhi 5 (17 Maghar\, Sambat 2084).\nSources: Sri Dasam Granth Sahib Ji (Bachitar Natak) (Adhyay 5\, Chhand 13–15 · Tilak Janju Rakha)\n\nJoti Jot Divas — Brahmgyani Baba Budha Ji (Ramdas) / ਜੋਤੀ ਜੋਤ ਦਿਵਸ — ਬ੍ਰਹਮਗਿਆਨੀ ਬਾਬਾ ਬੁੱਢਾ ਜੀ (ਰਮਦਾਸ)\n17 Maghar\, Sambat 2084 (Maghar Sudhi 4 tradition) · Passing of Brahmgyani Baba Budha Ji at Ramdas (Sambat 1688 Bikrami) in the physical presence of Sixth Patshah Sri Guru Hargobind Sahib Ji.\nSources: Sri Gur Pratap Suraj Granth (Raas 6\, Ansu 42–46 · Baba Budha Ji Joti Jot at Ramdas)\n\nShaheedi Divas — Bhai Mati Das Ji\, Bhai Sati Das Ji & Bhai Dayala Ji / ਸ਼ਹੀਦੀ ਦਿਵਸ — ਭਾਈ ਮਤੀ ਦਾਸ ਜੀ\, ਭਾਈ ਸਤੀ ਦਾਸ ਜੀ ਅਤੇ ਭਾਈ ਦਿਆਲਾ ਜੀ\nMaghar Sudhi 5 (17 Maghar\, Sambat 2084 · Chandni Chowk) · Unmatched martyrdom of Bhai Mati Das Ji (sawn alive reciting Japji Sahib)\, Bhai Dayala Ji (boiled in a cauldron)\, and Bhai Sati Das Ji (wrapped in cotton and set aflame) before Sri Guru Tegh Bahadur Sahib Ji in Delhi.\nSources: Bhatt Vahi Talauda & Sri Gur Pratap Suraj Granth (Raas 12\, Ansu 44–52 · Chandni Chowk Martyrs (Sambat 1732))\n\nhttps://calendar.tatkhalsa.in/
CATEGORIES:Tat Khalsa Puratan Jantri\,Daily Bikrami\,SHAHEEDI\,KHALSA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
