SUMMARY:25 Maghar 2084 · Maghar Sudhi 13 (Teras (Trayodashi)) (੨੫ ਮੱਘਰ ੨੦੮੪) — Janam Baba Atal Sahib Ji · Mata Sundri Ji
DESCRIPTION:Desi Solar Date: 25 Maghar\, Bikrami Sambat 2084 (੨੫ ਮੱਘਰ\, ਸੰਮਤ ੨੦੮੪)\nLunar Tithi: Maghar Sudhi 13 (Teras (Trayodashi)) · ਮੱਘਰ ਸੁਦੀ ੧੩ (ਤੇਰਸ)\nTithi ends (Sri Anandpur Sahib IST): 01:45 AM\, 12 Dec\n\nJanam Divas — Baba Atal Rai Sahib Ji / ਜਨਮ ਦਿਹਾੜਾ — ਬਾਬਾ ਅਟੱਲ ਰਾਇ ਸਾਹਿਬ ਜੀ\nMaghar Sudhi 13 (25 Maghar\, Sambat 2084) · Birth commemoration of Baba Atal Rai Ji (1676 Bikrami)\, luminous son of Sri Guru Hargobind Sahib Ji and Mata Nanaki Ji\, honored by the nine-story Gurdwara Baba Atal Sahib.\nSources: Sri Gurpratap Suraj Granth Sahib Ji (Raas 6\, Ansu 38–42 · Janam & Spiritual Glory of Baba Atal Rai Ji)\n\nJoti Jot Remembrance — Mata Sundri Ji (Delhi Panthic Leadership) / ਜੋਤੀ ਜੋਤ ਯਾਦਗਾਰ — ਮਾਤਾ ਸੁੰਦਰੀ ਜੀ (ਦਿੱਲੀ ਪੰਥਕ ਅਗਵਾਈ)\nMaghar Remembrance (25 Maghar\, Sambat 2084 · Mahan Kosh Note) · Honoring Mata Sundri Ji (Mata of Sahibzada Baba Ajit Singh Ji)\, who guided the Khalsa Panth for nearly four decades from Delhi and commissioned Bhai Mani Singh Ji’s seva at Sri Amritsar Sahib.\nSources: Mahan Kosh & Hukamnamas of Mata Sundri Ji (Entry: Sundri (Mata) · Sambat 1804 Delhi Archive)\n\nhttps://calendar.tatkhalsa.in/
CATEGORIES:Tat Khalsa Puratan Jantri\,Daily Bikrami\,GURPURAB\,KHALSA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
