UID:daily-2028-03-11@calendar.tatkhalsa.in
DTSTAMP:20260314T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20280311
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20280312
SUMMARY:28 Phagun 2084 · Chet Vadhi 1 (Ekam (Pratipada)) (੨੮ ਫੱਗਣ ੨੦੮੪) — Holla Mohalla · Delhi Fateh (1783)
DESCRIPTION:Desi Solar Date: 28 Phagun\, Bikrami Sambat 2084 (੨੮ ਫੱਗਣ\, ਸੰਮਤ ੨੦੮੪)\nLunar Tithi: Chet Vadhi 1 (Ekam (Pratipada)) · ਚੇਤ ਵਦੀ ੧ (ਏਕਮ)\nTithi ends (Sri Anandpur Sahib IST): 02:58 AM\, 12 Mar\n\nHolla Mohalla (Sri Anandpur Sahib) / ਹੋਲਾ ਮਹੱਲਾ (ਸ੍ਰੀ ਅਨੰਦਪੁਰ ਸਾਹਿਬ)\nChet Vadhi 1 (28 Phagun\, Sambat 2084) · Khalsa martial gathering at Sri Anandpur Sahib on Chet Vadhi 1 (28 Phagun\, Sambat 2084).\nSources: Sri Gur Pratap Suraj Granth (Rut 4\, Ansu 20–24 · Holgarh Fort)\n\nDelhi Fateh Divas — Baba Baghel Singh Ji & Sultan-ul-Qaum Sardar Jassa Singh Ahluwalia / ਦਿੱਲੀ ਫ਼ਤਹਿ ਦਿਵਸ — ਬਾਬਾ ਬਘੇਲ ਸਿੰਘ ਜੀ ਅਤੇ ਸੁਲਤਾਨ-ਉਲ-ਕੌਮ ਸਰਦਾਰ ਜੱਸਾ ਸਿੰਘ ਆਹਲੂਵਾਲੀਆ\n28 Phagun\, Sambat 2084 (11 March 1783 / Sambat 1839) · Khalsa conquest of the Red Fort in Delhi (Sambat 1839) led by Baba Baghel Singh Ji\, Sardar Jassa Singh Ahluwalia\, and Sardar Jassa Singh Ramgarhia\, establishing historic Delhi Gurdwaras.\nSources: Prachin Panth Prakash (Bhai Rattan Singh Bhangu) (Delhi Fateh & Gurdwara Seva · Phagun Sambat 1839)\n\nhttps://calendar.tatkhalsa.in/
CATEGORIES:Tat Khalsa Puratan Jantri\,Daily Bikrami\,KHALSA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
