SUMMARY:5 Poh 2085 · Poh Sudhi 4 (Chauth (Chaturthi)) (੫ ਪੋਹ ੨੦੮੫) — Mata Jito Ji Joti Jot
DESCRIPTION:Desi Solar Date: 5 Poh\, Bikrami Sambat 2085 (੫ ਪੋਹ\, ਸੰਮਤ ੨੦੮੫)\nLunar Tithi: Poh Sudhi 4 (Chauth (Chaturthi)) · ਪੋਹ ਸੁਦੀ ੪ (ਚੌਥ)\nTithi ends (Sri Anandpur Sahib IST): 07:47 AM\, 20 Dec\n\nJoti Jot Divas — Mata Jito Ji (Sri Anandpur Sahib) / ਜੋਤੀ ਜੋਤ ਦਿਵਸ — ਮਾਤਾ ਜੀਤੋ ਜੀ (ਸ੍ਰੀ ਅਨੰਦਪੁਰ ਸਾਹਿਬ)\n5 Poh\, Sambat 2085 · Passing of Mata Jito Ji (mother of Sahibzade Baba Jujhar Singh Ji\, Baba Zorawar Singh Ji & Baba Fateh Singh Ji) at Sri Anandpur Sahib (Agampura).\nSources: Bhatt Vahi & Guru Kian Sakhian (5 Poh\, Sambat 1757 · Agampura\, Sri Anandpur Sahib)\n\nhttps://calendar.tatkhalsa.in/
CATEGORIES:Tat Khalsa Puratan Jantri\,Daily Bikrami\,KHALSA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:daily-2028-12-21@calendar.tatkhalsa.in
DTSTAMP:20260314T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20281221
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20281222
SUMMARY:6 Poh 2085 · Poh Sudhi 5 (Panchmi) (੬ ਪੋਹ ੨੦੮੫) — Anandpur Qila Chhodna · Basant Ruth Arambh
DESCRIPTION:Desi Solar Date: 6 Poh\, Bikrami Sambat 2085 (੬ ਪੋਹ\, ਸੰਮਤ ੨੦੮੫)\nLunar Tithi: Poh Sudhi 5 (Panchmi) · ਪੋਹ ਸੁਦੀ ੫ (ਪੰਚਮੀ)\nTithi ends (Sri Anandpur Sahib IST): 09:24 AM\, 21 Dec\n\nShaheedi Hafta — Sri Anandpur Sahib Qila Chhodna (6–7 Poh) / ਸ਼ਹੀਦੀ ਹਫ਼ਤਾ — ਸ੍ਰੀ ਅਨੰਦਪੁਰ ਸਾਹਿਬ ਕਿਲ੍ਹਾ ਛੱਡਣਾ (੬–੭ ਪੋਹ)\n6 Poh\, Sambat 2085 · Opening of Shaheedi Hafta: after an eight-month siege\, Sri Guru Gobind Singh Ji\, the Guru Ghar Parivar\, and the Khalsa evacuated Qila Anandgarh on the freezing night of 6–7 Poh\, Sambat 1761.\nSources: Bhatt Vahi Talauda & Prachin Panth Prakash (6–7 Poh\, Sambat 1761 · Evacuation of Qila Anandgarh)\n\nBasant Ruth Arambh (Inauguration of Raag Basant Kirtan) / ਬਸੰਤ ਰੁੱਤ ਆਰੰਭ (ਰਾਗ ਬਸੰਤ ਕੀਰਤਨ ਦੀ ਸ਼ੁਰੂਆਤ)\nPoh Sudhi 5 (6 Poh\, Sambat 2085) · Puratan Gurdwara Maryada marking the commencement of Raag Basant Kirtan (Lohri / Maghi eve) through Holla Mohalla at Sachkhand Sri Harmandir Sahib and all Takhts.\nSources: Sri Guru Granth Sahib Ji (Ang 1176 · Raag Basant Mahalla 3 (Basant Ki Vaar & Seasonal Renewal))\n\nhttps://calendar.tatkhalsa.in/
CATEGORIES:Tat Khalsa Puratan Jantri\,Daily Bikrami\,SHAHEEDI\,KHALSA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:daily-2028-12-22@calendar.tatkhalsa.in
DTSTAMP:20260314T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20281222
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20281223
SUMMARY:7 Poh 2085 · Poh Sudhi 6 (Chhat (Shashthi)) (੭ ਪੋਹ ੨੦੮੫) — Sarsa Nadi & Bhai Uday/Bachittar Singh
DESCRIPTION:Desi Solar Date: 7 Poh\, Bikrami Sambat 2085 (੭ ਪੋਹ\, ਸੰਮਤ ੨੦੮੫)\nLunar Tithi: Poh Sudhi 6 (Chhat (Shashthi)) · ਪੋਹ ਸੁਦੀ ੬ (ਛਠ)\nTithi ends (Sri Anandpur Sahib IST): 11:32 AM\, 22 Dec\n\nShaheedi Hafta — Sarsa Nadi Vichhora\, Bhai Uday Singh Ji & Bhai Bachittar Singh Ji / ਸ਼ਹੀਦੀ ਹਫ਼ਤਾ — ਸਰਸਾ ਨਦੀ ਵਿਛੋੜਾ\, ਭਾਈ ਉਦੈ ਸਿੰਘ ਜੀ ਅਤੇ ਭਾਈ ਬਚਿੱਤਰ ਸਿੰਘ ਜੀ\n7 Poh\, Sambat 2085 · Separation of Guru Gobind Singh Ji’s family at the flooded Sarsa River (Parivar Vichhora)\, Asa Di Vaar amid battle\, and the legendary martyrdom of Bhai Uday Singh Ji (Shahi Tibbi) and Bhai Bachittar Singh Ji (Malikpur/Kotla Nihang).\nSources: Bhatt Vahi Multani Sindhi & Sri Gur Pratap Suraj Granth (Ayan 2\, Ansu 1–12 · Sarsa Nadi\, Shahi Tibbi & Kotla Nihang (7 Poh 1761))\n\nhttps://calendar.tatkhalsa.in/
CATEGORIES:Tat Khalsa Puratan Jantri\,Daily Bikrami\,SHAHEEDI
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:daily-2028-12-23@calendar.tatkhalsa.in
DTSTAMP:20260314T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20281223
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20281224
SUMMARY:8 Poh 2085 · Poh Sudhi 7 (Saptami) (੮ ਪੋਹ ੨੦੮੫) — Shaheedi Vadde Sahibzade · Three Panj Pyare (Chamkaur) · Parkash Guru Gobind Singh Ji
DESCRIPTION:Desi Solar Date: 8 Poh\, Bikrami Sambat 2085 (੮ ਪੋਹ\, ਸੰਮਤ ੨੦੮੫)\nLunar Tithi: Poh Sudhi 7 (Saptami) · ਪੋਹ ਸੁਦੀ ੭ (ਸਪਤਮੀ)\nTithi ends (Sri Anandpur Sahib IST): 01:59 PM\, 23 Dec\n\nShaheedi Divas — Vadde Sahibzade (Sri Chamkaur Sahib) / ਸ਼ਹੀਦੀ ਦਿਵਸ — ਵੱਡੇ ਸਾਹਿਬਜ਼ਾਦੇ (ਸ੍ਰੀ ਚਮਕੌਰ ਸਾਹਿਬ)\n8 Poh\, Sambat 2085 · Martyrdom of Baba Ajit Singh Ji\, Baba Jujhar Singh Ji\, and the Singhs of Garhi Chamkaur (8 Poh\, 1761 Bikrami).\nSources: Sri Dasam Granth Sahib Ji (Zafarnama) (Verses 19–22 & 78 · Battle of Chamkaur & Four Sons) | Prachin Panth Prakash (Rattan Singh Bhangu) (Sakhi Garhi Chamkaur · 8 Poh 1761 Bikrami)\n\nShaheedi Divas — Three Panj Pyare (Bhai Himmat Singh\, Bhai Mohkam Singh & Bhai Sahib Singh Ji) / ਸ਼ਹੀਦੀ ਦਿਵਸ — ਤਿੰਨ ਪੰਜ ਪਿਆਰੇ (ਭਾਈ ਹਿੰਮਤ ਸਿੰਘ\, ਭਾਈ ਮੋਹਕਮ ਸਿੰਘ ਅਤੇ ਭਾਈ ਸਾਹਿਬ ਸਿੰਘ ਜੀ)\n8 Poh\, Sambat 2085 · Supreme martyrdom of three of the original Panj Pyare—Bhai Himmat Singh Ji (Jagannath Puri)\, Bhai Mohkam Singh Ji (Dwarka)\, and Bhai Sahib Singh Ji (Bidar)—alongside the Vadde Sahibzade and 40 Singhs at Garhi Chamkaur.\nSources: Bhatt Vahi Talauda & Prachin Panth Prakash (8 Poh\, Sambat 1761 · Garhi Sri Chamkaur Sahib Martyrs)\n\nParkash Purab — Sri Guru Gobind Singh Ji / ਪ੍ਰਕਾਸ਼ ਪੁਰਬ — ਸ੍ਰੀ ਗੁਰੂ ਗੋਬਿੰਦ ਸਿੰਘ ਜੀ\nPoh Sudhi 7 (8 Poh\, Sambat 2085) · Sacred Parkash Purab of Dashmesh Pita Sri Guru Gobind Singh Ji at Takht Sri Patna Sahib (Poh Sudhi 7\, 1723 Bikrami).\nSources: Sri Dasam Granth Sahib Ji (Bachitar Natak) (Adhyay 7 · Tahi Parkash Hamara Bhayo\, Patna Shehar Bikhai Bhav Layo) | Hukamnamas of Sri Guru Tegh Bahadur Ji & Bhatt Vahis (Patna Sangat Hukamnamas · Poh Sudhi Saptami 1723 Bikrami)\n\nhttps://calendar.tatkhalsa.in/
CATEGORIES:Tat Khalsa Puratan Jantri\,Daily Bikrami\,SHAHEEDI\,GURPURAB
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
