SUMMARY:6 Phagun 2086 · Magh Puranmashi (੬ ਫੱਗਣ ੨੦੮੬) — Parkash Bhagat Ravidas Ji · Bhagat Ravidas Ji Parkash
DESCRIPTION:Desi Solar Date: 6 Phagun\, Bikrami Sambat 2086 (੬ ਫੱਗਣ\, ਸੰਮਤ ੨੦੮੬)\nLunar Tithi: Magh Sudhi 15 (Puranmashi) · ਮਾਘ ਸੁਦੀ ੧੫ (ਪੂਰਨਮਾਸ਼ੀ)\nTithi ends (Sri Anandpur Sahib IST): 11:51 AM\, 18 Feb\n\nParkash Purab — Bhagat Ravidas Ji / ਪ੍ਰਕਾਸ਼ ਪੁਰਬ — ਭਗਤ ਰਵਿਦਾਸ ਜੀ\nMagh Puranmashi (6 Phagun\, Sambat 2086) · Commemoration of Bhagat Ravidas Ji\, whose 41 hymns in Sri Guru Granth Sahib Ji envision Begampura\, the city without sorrow.\nSources: Sri Guru Granth Sahib Ji (Ang 345 · Raag Gauri Bani Bhagat Ravidas Ji)\n\nParkash Purab — Bhagat Ravidas Ji (SGGS 41 Shabads) / ਪ੍ਰਕਾਸ਼ ਪੁਰਬ — ਭਗਤ ਰਵਿਦਾਸ ਜੀ (ਸ੍ਰੀ ਗੁਰੂ ਗ੍ਰੰਥ ਸਾਹਿਬ ੪੧ ਸ਼ਬਦ)\nMagh Puranmashi (6 Phagun\, Sambat 2086) · Parkash Purab of Shiromani Bhagat Ravidas Ji on Magh Puranmashi (28 Magh\, Sambat 2086)\, visionary of Begampura (SGGS Ang 345).\nSources: Sri Guru Granth Sahib Ji (Ang 345 · Raag Gauri\, Bhagat Ravidas Ji (Begampura))\n\nhttps://calendar.tatkhalsa.in/
CATEGORIES:Tat Khalsa Puratan Jantri\,Daily Bikrami\,Puranmashi\,KHALSA\,GURPURAB
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:daily-2030-02-19@calendar.tatkhalsa.in
DTSTAMP:20260314T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20300219
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20300220
SUMMARY:7 Phagun 2086 · Phagun Vadhi 1 (Ekam (Pratipada)) (੭ ਫੱਗਣ ੨੦੮੬) — Saka Sri Nankana Sahib
DESCRIPTION:Desi Solar Date: 7 Phagun\, Bikrami Sambat 2086 (੭ ਫੱਗਣ\, ਸੰਮਤ ੨੦੮੬)\nLunar Tithi: Phagun Vadhi 1 (Ekam (Pratipada)) · ਫੱਗਣ ਵਦੀ ੧ (ਏਕਮ)\nTithi ends (Sri Anandpur Sahib IST): 10:06 AM\, 19 Feb\n\nShaheedi Saka Sri Nankana Sahib (Bhai Lachhman Singh Ji Dharowali & Shaheed Jatha) / ਸ਼ਹੀਦੀ ਸਾਕਾ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਨਨਕਾਣਾ ਸਾਹਿਬ (ਭਾਈ ਲਛਮਣ ਸਿੰਘ ਜੀ ਧਾਰੋਵਾਲੀ ਅਤੇ ਸ਼ਹੀਦ ਜਥਾ)\nPhagun Vadhi 1 (7 Phagun\, Sambat 2086) · Supreme peaceful martyrdom of Bhai Lachhman Singh Ji Dharowali\, Bhai Dalip Singh Ji\, and over 130 Singhs on 20–21 February 1921 liberating Gurdwara Janam Asthan Sri Nankana Sahib.\nSources: Sri Guru Granth Sahib Ji (Ang 1412 · Salok Vaaran Te Vadhik (Mahalla 1)) | Saka Nankana Sahib Historical Chronicle (SGPC / Gurdwara Sudhar Lehar) (Phagun 1977 Bikrami (20–21 Feb 1921) · Liberation of Janam Asthan Sri Nankana Sahib)\n\nhttps://calendar.tatkhalsa.in/
CATEGORIES:Tat Khalsa Puratan Jantri\,Daily Bikrami\,SHAHEEDI
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
